/*
:name: removed_spawn_statement
:type: error
:error: `spawn` was removed
:help: move the body into the enclosing `test` block
*/

// The STATEMENT form (removed_spawn.prp pins the call form). `spawn`/`join`/
// `cancel` are gone (docs/pyrope/09-verification.md): a testbench is one
// deterministic `tick`/`step` loop. The pinned grammar still parses the
// statement, so the front end refuses it outright instead of minting the empty
// sim-only comb it used to (0 errors, body never lowered).
test spawn_removed {
  spawn job = { assert(true) }  // locate_error_here
}
